        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Extract Destination Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770881525154"
          },
          "code": "DESTINATION_ATTRIBUTES_EXTRACTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770620389634",
          "id": "1770641581007",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770641581008_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "###Objective \nExtract destination (target/receiving) attribute values for a project cost transfer/adjustment from the user’s input message. \n\n###Inputs \n    current user message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n    lastAIResponse: {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvLastAIResponse}}.\n    expectedInput: {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvExpectedInput}}.\n     \n###Allowed Destination Attributes (extract only these) \n    Project  \n    Task  \n    ExpenditureType  \n    ProjectRoleName  \n    Justification  \n    Contract  \n    FundingSource\n    Quantity\n     \n###Destination Synonyms / Naming Variations \n\n1. Treat these terms as indicating destination/target/receiving information (where costs should be moved to): \n\n    destination, target, receiving, receiver\n    “to”, “move to”, “transfer to”, “charge to”, “reclass to”\n    new / updated / corrected (project/task/etc.)\n    apply to, post to, book to, allocate to\n    “into …”, “onto …”, “under …”\n    “target attributes”, “destination attributes”, “receiving attributes”, “to attributes”, “new attributes”, “corrected attributes”\n     \n\nDo not extract source values (e.g., “from/current/source/existing”) unless the message clearly states they are destination/target values. \nTask \n\n From the current user message, extract only the values of the allowed destination attributes when the user is specifying destination/target details. \nSource vs Destination rule \n\n If the user provides both source and destination (e.g., “from Project P1 … to Project P2 …”), extract only the destination/target side (e.g., Project P2), and ignore the source side. \n\n2. Special State Handling\n    2a.When expectedInput = \"NEED_TARGET_INFO\"\n            Treat any recognized allowed destination attributes in the message as destination by default unless they are explicitly marked as source (e.g., preceded by “from”, “source”, “current”).\n    2b.When expectedInput = \"NEED_SOURCE_TXN\"\n            If an attribute is not mentioned as destination or target explicitly at this stage, do not consider it as destination attribute, consider it as ambiguous and omit.\n\n3. Amount values if provided can not be extracted as Quantity. Amount and quantity are different. Quantity can be extracted only if the user input mentions the value as quantity or implicit attribute mapping.\n\n4. Chat History Usage (implicit attribute mapping) \nUse lastAIResponse to interpret short/partial replies. \n\nImplicit destination attribute mapping rule:\n           If lastAIResponse asks for a specific missing destination attribute (for example:“Please provide a valid target Task information”), then treat the user’s current inputMessage as the value for that requested attribute even if the user does not explicitly name the attribute. \n           Apply this for any of the allowed destination attributes: Project, Task, ExpenditureType, ProjectRoleName, Justification, Contract, FundingSource, Quantity\n           Examples of AI prompts that should trigger mapping (non-exhaustive): \n                   “Please provide a valid target Task information.”\n                   “Provide the destination Project.”\n                   “Enter a valid target Expenditure Type.”\n                   “What is the target Contract?”\n                   “Please share the receiving Funding Source.”\n                   “Provide the target Project Role Name.”\n                   “Please provide a justification.”\n                   \"Please provide the quantity.”\n          If lastAIResponse requests multiple destination attributes, only map the user’s input to the attribute(s) by the keyword in user input; otherwise extract none or only the clearly matching one.\n     \n###Output \nCreate an output object named destinationAttributes. \nOutput rules:\n    Include only the attributes that you successfully extracted (do not include keys with blank/empty values).\n    If no destination attribute values are present in the current message (and none can be inferred via the chat-history mapping rule), output an empty object:\n        destinationAttributes = {}\n\nalso add an attribute \"explanation\" in the output destinationAttributes object with the explanation on how you came up with the result for the current user input based on the above rules.\n         \n###Examples (Sample Only) \n\nInput: “Move costs from Project P1 Task T1 to Project P2 Task T2 with justification ‘charged to a different task’.”\nOutput:\ndestinationAttributes = { \"Project\": \"P2\", \"Task\": \"T2\", \"Justification\": \"charged to a different task\" } \n\nInput: “I want to transfer a cost in Project P1 Task T1.”\nOutput:\ndestinationAttributes = {} \n\nInput: “I want to transfer a cost in Project P1 Task T1 to the Business Unit ABC”\nOutput:\ndestinationAttributes = {}\n\nChat-history implied mapping:   \n\n    lastAIResponse: “Please provide a valid target Task information”  \n    inputMessage: “T2”\n    Output:\n    destinationAttributes = { \"Task\": \"T2\" }\n\n    lastAIResponse: “Please provide target Contract information”  \n    inputMessage: “Contract is ABC”\n    Output:\n    destinationAttributes = { \"Contract\": \"ABC\" }"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "\"destinationAttributes\": {\n        }",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1774600841996",
            "name": "Fill Destination Attributes",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var destinationAttributes = $context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvAdjustmentAttributes; \nif($context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvAdjustmentAttributes == null || $context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvAdjustmentAttributes == \"\"){\n   destinationAttributes = {};\n}\nvar newlyParsed =  $context.$nodes.DESTINATION_ATTRIBUTES_EXTRACTOR.$output.destinationAttributes;\nvar attributes = [\"Project\", \"Task\", \"ExpenditureType\", \"ProjectRoleName\", \"Justification\" , \"Contract\", \"FundingSource\", \"Quantity\"];\nfor(let i=0; i<8; i++){\n    if(newlyParsed[attributes[i]] == null || newlyParsed[attributes[i]] === \"\") continue;\n    destinationAttributes[attributes[i]] = newlyParsed[attributes[i]];\n}\nreturn destinationAttributes;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770705683132"
          },
          "code": "FILL_DESTINATION_ATTRIBUTES",
          "id": "1770881525154",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1774600841996",
            "name": "Set Destination Attributes"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772517883393"
          },
          "code": "SET_DESTINATION_ATTRIBUTES",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770620389634",
          "id": "1770705683132",
          "inputs": [
            {
