          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770636514000_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "###Objective \nDetermine whether the user’s message contains any valid criteria based on Project Cost Attributes, and respond with the correct fixed message. \nRules contain exact text message you need to disply in HTML format, you just need to render the HTML.\n\n###Inputs \n\n    {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} is the user’s message  \n    {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvProjectCostAttributes}} is the list of valid projectCostAttributes (names/labels)\n     \n###Task / Decision Rules \n     \n1. Detect criteria based on projectCostAttributes\n      Check whether the user’s message includes any criteria that matches any item in projectCostAttributes, using:   \n        Exact match (same attribute name/label)  \n        Classic/alias match (common alternate names)  \n        Fuzzy match (partial match, spacing/punctuation variations, common synonyms/abbreviations, minor misspellings)\n         \n2. Criteria must include an intended value (broadly interpreted)\n      If an attribute match is found, treat it as user-provided criteria if the user appears to provide any associated value with the intent to filter (e.g., “Project = …”, “Txn Date …”, “Supplier …”, “Amount > …”).\n      Even if the value is ambiguous, unrecognizable, conflicting, incomplete, or contradictory, still treat it as the user intending to provide a value. \n     \n3. If criteria is detected (rule 1 + rule 2), respond exactly with:\n    `<p>I couldn’t find a transaction that matches the details you entered.<br><br>To continue, do one of the following:<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li> Send a complete request. For example: Transfer transaction 17285 to project 100, task 11. </li><li>Provide project, task, and transaction date to help me identify the transaction first.</li></ul><br>Need a template? Say \"Show templates for project cost transfer\" or \"Show templates for finding transactions\".</p>`\n     \n4. If no projectCostAttributes criteria is detected, but the message indicates a request for a single project cost transfer/adjustment (single transaction), respond exactly with:\n    `<p>I can help with a single project cost transfer.<br><br>To continue, do one of the following:<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li> Send a complete request. For example: Transfer transaction 17285 to project 100, task 11. </li><li>Provide project, task, and transaction date to help me identify the transaction first.</li></ul><br>Need a template? Say \"Show templates for project cost transfer\" or \"Show templates for finding transactions\".</p>` \n     \n     \n###Output Requirements \n    Output only one of the exact strings above.  \n    Do not output JSON, tables, explanations, or any other text."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
