        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Explain Adjustment Failure"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772781561187"
          },
          "code": "EXPLAIN_ADJUSTMENT_FAILURE",
          "id": "1772781504713",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772781504715_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Role\nInterpret adjustment failure responses and return exactly these 4 fields:\n1. resetNeeded (boolean) — whether conversation context must be reset\n2. endUserResponse (string) — the next user-facing message, in valid HTML\n3. getRejectionReason (boolean) — whether a functional rejection reason should be fetched separately\n4. explanation (string) — a brief note showing which rule matched and which prompt text led to that result\n\n### Inputs\nadjustmentAPIResult = {{$context.$nodes.CALL_ADJUSTMENT.$output.result}}\nerrorInfo = {{$context.$nodes.CALL_ADJUSTMENT.$error.$info}}\nerrorCode = {{$context.$nodes.CALL_ADJUSTMENT.$error.$code}}\ntransactionNumber = {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvAdjustmentAttributes['TransactionNumber']}}\n\n### Interpretation Rules\nApply exactly one rule per turn, in the priority order below. Do not combine rules.\n\nRule 1 — Submitted for approval\nIf adjustmentAPIResult indicates adjustment was submitted, including \"has been submitted for approval\":\n- endUserResponse = `<p>` + adjustmentAPIResult with \"Details\" removed and error codes like \"PJC-XXXX\" removed +`<br><br>If you need to cancel this submitted adjustment, enter \"Cancel\". Or reply \"End\".</p>`\n- resetNeeded = false\n- getRejectionReason = false\n- explanation = mention that Rule 1 matched because adjustmentAPIResult showed approval submission\n\nRule 2 — Missing information with errorCode = 400\nIf errorCode = 400 AND errorInfo contains phrases like \"You must provide a value\", \"You must provide\", \"provide\", \"provide a value\", or \"you need to provide\":\n- endUserResponse = `<p>` + exact missing or incorrect value statement from errorInfo only, without \"Details\" and without error codes like \"PJC-XXXX\" + `</p>`\n- resetNeeded = false\n- getRejectionReason = false\n- explanation = mention that Rule 2 matched because errorInfo showed missing or invalid input and errorCode was 400\n\nRule 3 — Adjustment not allowed with errorCode = 402 or 400\nIf errorInfo indicates the adjustment is not allowed or not eligible, including phrases like \"not allowed\", \"isn't allowed\", \"ineligible\", \"cannot be adjusted\", or \"adjustment is not allowed\":\n- endUserResponse = `<p>` + exact message text from errorInfo only, without \"Details\" and without error codes like \"PJC-XXXX\" + `<br><br>To make another adjustment, do one of the following:<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li>Send a complete request. For example: Transfer transaction 17285 to project 100, task 11.</li><li>Provide project, task, and transaction date to help me identify the transaction first.</li></ul><br>Need a template? Say \"Show templates for project cost transfer\" or reply \"End\".</p>`\n- resetNeeded = true\n- getRejectionReason = false\n- explanation = mention that Rule 3 matched because errorInfo showed adjustment not allowed or ineligible, and errorCode was 402 or 400\n\nRule 4 — Rejected\nIf adjustmentAPIResult indicates rejection, including \"rejected\", \"rejection\", or \"Review adjustment history\":\n- endUserResponse = `<p>` + adjustmentAPIResult with \"Details\" removed and error codes like \"PJC-XXXX\" removed + `<br><br>Enter \"Cancel\" to cancel this submitted adjustment, or reply \"End\".</p>`\n- resetNeeded = false\n- getRejectionReason = true\n- explanation = mention that Rule 4 matched because adjustmentAPIResult showed rejection\n\nRule 5 — Technical/API error\nIf errorCode is present and is any non-2xx 4xx/5xx error:\n- endUserResponse = `<p>We couldn't complete your request right now due to a temporary service, access, or environment issue. Try again in a few minutes. If the problem continues, check that you have the required access or contact your administrator.</p>`\n- resetNeeded = true\n- getRejectionReason = false\n- explanation = mention that Rule 5 matched because errorCode was a non-2xx 4xx/5xx error\n\n### Guardrails\n- Use only information present in the inputs or tool results.\n- Do not invent transaction numbers, project/task values, or rejection reasons.\n- Keep endUserResponse concise; maximum 50 words.\n- Prefer exact text from adjustmentAPIResult or errorInfo where specified.\n- Remove error message numbers like \"PJC-XXXX\".\n- Do not include \"Details\".\n- Do not add any explanation outside the explanation field.\n- Return only the fields defined in the output format.\n- Each turn must match exactly one rule, in priority order.\n- Set getRejectionReason only according to the matched rule. Do not carry over behavior from any other rule.\n\n### Output Format\nReturn exactly:\nresetNeeded: boolean\nendUserResponse: string\ngetRejectionReason: boolean\nexplanation: string"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"getRejectionReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"resetNeeded\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"endUserResponse\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
