          "code": "DISPLAY_MORE_THAN_THRESHOLD",
          "id": "1773313640919",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773313640920_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "###Task\nShow the HTML exactly as provided in input.\n\n###Input\nHTML code: {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_MORE_THAN_THRESHOLD_MESSAGE.$output.result}}\nDeeplink: {{$context.$nodes.GET_MPC_DEEPLINK.$output}} \n\n###Output Format\nEmbed the Deeplink on the text \"Manage Project Costs\" while displaying.\nMake sure to add the target=\"_blank\" for <a> tag while showing the deeplink."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Summarize Criteria"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771408706738"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_CRITERIA",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771408706738",
          "id": "1773244066258",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773244066259_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "###Objective\nYou are an assistant that generates a user-facing summary of the filters currently applied to a dataset. \n\n###Goal\nGiven (1) the combined user messages and (2) the SQL WHERE-clause fragment, produce a single short, natural-language sentence describing only the filters that are actually applied. \n\n###Inputs \n {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvUserMessages}} \n {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_IDENTIFICATION_DETAILS.$output.filterFormed}} \n {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvProjectCostAttrDisplayNames}} \n\n###Rules \n     The SQL Filter Clause (filterFormed) is the single source of truth for which filters are applied.\n     Describe only filters that appear in the SQL Filter Clause (filterFormed).\n     Ignore any details from User Messages that are not reflected in the SQL Filter Clause (filterFormed).\n     Output must be criteria-only (a label/value list). Do not add any narrative/leading text such as: “Cost transactions in”, “Transactions for”, “I found”, “Showing”, “Below”, “Please select”, etc.  \n     The output must start with a criterion label (e.g., “Project”, “Task”, “Business Unit”, “Accounting Period”) and then the value. Never start with a verb.\n     Do not output SQL syntax (e.g., AND, OR, =, parentheses, quotes) and avoid exposing raw column/field names if they look technical.\n     Prefer the user’s wording when naming a filter:\n        If User Messages contain a clear label/phrase that matches a SQL filter, reuse it (or a very close paraphrase). Just correct the cpitalization as needed.\n         \n     Do not invent new labels when a suitable phrase already exists in User Messages.\n     If no suitable phrase exists in User Messages for a filter, create a simple, human-friendly label (e.g., “Created Time\", \"Accounting Period\").\n     Output must be exactly one line and one sentence (no bullets, no lists, no multiple sentences).\n     Combine all applied filters into a coherent, natural sentence.\n     Do not mention SQL, queries, or system behavior (e.g., don’t say “filters applied” or “based on the query”).\n     If the SQL Filter Clause contains no actual filter conditions, output exactly:\n        No filters are currently applied.\n    The output can NOT logically have same attribute twice with same or different values.\n    Output Format: 1. Use DisplayNames object to get the display names of the attributes you included in the criteriaSummary. DisplayNames contains display names as key and attributes list as values for each display name 2. For each attribute, pick up the display name from this object and have it in criteriaSummary. 3. In the output, add <b> tag to highlight only the values for each attribute when displayed. For example: Project: <b>P1</b>.\n     \n\n###Output \n\nReturn the final user-facing sentence in \"criteriaSummary\" output. \nand also explain how you came with the result from inputs. provide this in output \"explanation\".\n\n\n###Example \n\nInput User Messages:\n“1. I want to transfer a cost in Project P1, Business Unit Vision Operations (USA) 2. And the accounting period is Feb-26”. \n\nInput SQL Filter Clause:\nand (projectNumber = 'P1' or projectName = 'P1') and businessUnitName = 'Vision Operations (USA)'\n\nOutput:\nProject: <b>P1</b> , Business Unit: <b>Vision Operations (USA)</b>"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"explanation\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"criteriaSummary\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1774600841996",
            "name": "Generate Success Response",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let identifiedProjectCostDetails = $context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvIdentifiedProjectCostDetails;\nlet adjustmentAttributes = $context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvAdjustmentAttributes;\nlet adjustmentCallResponse = $context.$nodes.CALL_ADJUSTMENT.$output;\n\nlet costDetail = identifiedProjectCostDetails[0] || {};\nlet transactionNumber = costDetail.TRANSACTIONNUMBER || null;\nlet projectNumberFrom = costDetail.PROJECTNUMBER || null;\nlet projectNameFrom = costDetail.PROJECTNAME || null;\nlet taskNumberFrom = costDetail.TASKNUMBER || null;\nlet taskNameFrom = costDetail.TASKNAME || null;\nlet fundingSourceNumberFrom = costDetail.FUNDINGSOURCENUMBER || null;\nlet fundingSourceNameFrom = costDetail.FUNDINGSOURCENAME || null;\nlet contractNumberFrom = costDetail.CONTRACTNUMBER || null;\nlet contractNameFrom = costDetail.CONTRACTNAME || null;\nlet projectRoleNameFrom = costDetail.PROJECTROLENAME || null;\nlet projectCostTypeFrom = costDetail.PROJECTCOSTTYPENAME || null;\nlet transactionDateStr = costDetail.TRANSACTIONDATE || null;\nlet formattedDate = null;\nif (transactionDateStr) {\n  let transactionDate = new Date(transactionDateStr);\n  formattedDate = transactionDate.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: '2-digit', day: '2-digit', year: 'numeric' });\n}\n\nlet adjustedTransactionNumber = null;\nif (adjustmentCallResponse) {\n  let responseStr = (adjustmentCallResponse.result || adjustmentCallResponse).toString();\n  const regex = /transaction number[s]?\\s+(\\d+)/gi;\n  let match;\n  let lastMatch = null;\n  while ((match = regex.exec(responseStr)) !== null) {\n    lastMatch = match[1];\n  }\n  adjustedTransactionNumber = lastMatch;\n}\n\nlet toProjectNumber = adjustmentAttributes.ProjectNumber || adjustmentAttributes.Project || null;\nlet toProjectName = adjustmentAttributes.ProjectName || null;\nlet toTaskNumber = adjustmentAttributes.TaskNumber || adjustmentAttributes.Task || null;\nlet toTaskName = adjustmentAttributes.TaskName || null;\nlet toFundingSourceNumber = adjustmentAttributes.FundingSourceNumber || null;\nlet toFundingSourceName = adjustmentAttributes.FundingSourceName || null;\nlet toContractNumber = adjustmentAttributes.ContractNumber || adjustmentAttributes.Contract || null;\nlet toContractName = adjustmentAttributes.ContractName || null;\nlet toProjectRoleName = adjustmentAttributes.ProjectRoleName || adjustmentAttributes.ProjectRole || null;\nlet toProjectCostType = adjustmentAttributes.ProjectCostType || adjustmentAttributes.ExpenditureType || null;\n\nlet useProjectName = !!toProjectName;\nlet projectFrom = useProjectName ? projectNameFrom : projectNumberFrom;\nlet projectTo = useProjectName ? toProjectName : toProjectNumber;\n\nlet useTaskName = !!toTaskName;\nlet taskFrom = useTaskName ? taskNameFrom : taskNumberFrom;\nlet taskTo = useTaskName ? toTaskName : toTaskNumber;\n\nlet useFundingName = !!toFundingSourceName;\nlet fundingFrom = useFundingName ? fundingSourceNameFrom : fundingSourceNumberFrom;\nlet fundingTo = useFundingName ? toFundingSourceName : toFundingSourceNumber;\n\nlet useContractName = !!toContractName;\nlet contractFrom = useContractName ? contractNameFrom : contractNumberFrom;\nlet contractTo = useContractName ? toContractName : toContractNumber;\n\nlet hasProject = !!projectTo;\nlet hasTask = !!taskTo;\nlet hasFunding = !!fundingTo;\nlet hasContract = !!contractTo;\nlet hasProjectRole = !!toProjectRoleName;\nlet hasProjectCostType = !!toProjectCostType;\n\nlet successResponse = null;\nif (hasProject && hasTask && hasFunding && hasContract) {\n  successResponse = `Transfer completed successfully. Transaction ${transactionNumber} was transferred. <br><br>From: <br>Project ${projectFrom}/Task ${taskFrom}/FundingSource ${fundingFrom}/Contract ${contractFrom} <br><br>To: <br>Project ${projectTo}/Task ${taskTo}/FundingSource ${fundingTo}/Contract ${contractTo} <br><br>Adjusted transaction number: <b>${adjustedTransactionNumber}</b>. <br><br>To make another adjustment, do one of the following:<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li> Send a complete request. For example: Transfer transaction 17285 to project 100, task 11. </li><li>Provide project, task, and transaction date to help me identify the transaction first.</li></ul><br>Need a template? Say \"Show templates for project cost transfer\" or \"Show templates for finding transactions\".`;\n} else if (hasProject && hasTask) {\n  successResponse = `Transfer completed successfully. Transaction ${transactionNumber} was transferred. <br><br>From:<br> Project ${projectFrom}/Task ${taskFrom} <br><br>To: <br>Project ${projectTo}/Task ${taskTo}  <br><br>Adjusted transaction number: <b>${adjustedTransactionNumber}</b>. <br><br>To make another adjustment, do one of the following:<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li> Send a complete request. For example: Transfer transaction 17285 to project 100, task 11. </li><li>Provide project, task, and transaction date to help me identify the transaction first.</li></ul><br>Need a template? Say \"Show templates for project cost transfer\" or \"Show templates for finding transactions\".`;\n} else if (hasProjectRole) {\n  let fromRolePart = projectRoleNameFrom ? `<br><br>From: <br>Project Role ${projectRoleNameFrom} ` : '';\n  successResponse = `Transfer completed successfully. Transaction ${transactionNumber} was transferred. ${fromRolePart} <br><br>To:<br> Project Role ${toProjectRoleName} <br><br>Adjusted transaction number: <b>${adjustedTransactionNumber}</b>. <br><br>To make another adjustment, do one of the following:<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li> Send a complete request. For example: Transfer transaction 17285 to project 100, task 11. </li><li>Provide project, task, and transaction date to help me identify the transaction first.</li></ul><br>Need a template? Say \"Show templates for project cost transfer\" or \"Show templates for finding transactions\".`;\n} else if (hasProjectCostType) {\n  successResponse = `Transfer completed successfully. Transaction ${transactionNumber} was transferred. <br><br> From: <br>Expenditure type ${projectCostTypeFrom} <br><br>To:<br>Expenditure type ${toProjectCostType} <br><br>Adjusted transaction number: <b>${adjustedTransactionNumber}</b>. <br><br>To make another adjustment, do one of the following:<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\"><li> Send a complete request. For example: Transfer transaction 17285 to project 100, task 11. </li><li>Provide project, task, and transaction date to help me identify the transaction first.</li></ul><br>Need a template? Say \"Show templates for project cost transfer\" or \"Show templates for finding transactions\".`;\n}\n\nreturn `<p>`+successResponse+ `</p>`;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770804004447"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_SUCCESS_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1773374376072",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
